@app.cell(hide_code=True)
def _(figures_view, flows, hurdle, money, rate, social):
    mo.md(
        f"""## 14. What the arithmetic says

        Charge the soft schedule for its money properly, at the stance rate of {rate(social)} and priced
        against a hurdle of {rate(hurdle)}, and the farm is worth
        **{money(financing_neutral(figures_view))}**. Discount the same flows at the fund's own hurdle
        instead and it is worth **{money(financing_neutral(view(flows, SHEET, hurdle, hurdle)))}** -
        the identical farm, the identical landscape, the difference being only who is doing the
        discounting and at what rate.

        Bring the subsidy in and the blend reaches **{money(blended(view(flows, SHEET, hurdle, hurdle)))}**
        at the hurdle. That is the sentence the case has to answer: the gap does not close when the
        subsidy and the shortfall are discounted at one rate, and the workbook does not let the
        comparison be made at two.

        So the question worth arguing is not whether blended finance fails here - it is which of the
        numbers underneath it the case actually stands behind: the 50 hectares its text describes or the
        55 its spreadsheet assumes, the 25-year amortisation the page states or the 30 the model runs,
        and a hurdle rate of {rate(hurdle)} that is claimed rather than sourced. Section 8 prices the
        first two; the third moves every verdict on this page the moment you drag it.
    """
    )


@app.cell(hide_code=True)
def _():
    mo.md(
        f"""## 15. Provenance and limits

        Built {pack['frozen_at']} by `data/build_web.py`. Digests of what it was generated from:
        `layering {pack['sources']['layering']}`, `engine {pack['sources']['engine']}`,
        `reactor {pack['sources']['reactor']}`, `stances {pack['sources']['stances']}`,
        `criteria {pack['sources']['criteria']}`, `tensions {pack['sources']['tensions']}`.

        The generator asserts its own verdicts against `build_criteria.verdict_rows()` for every
        scoreable stance and refuses to write this file if the two disagree by more than 1e-6. The
        arithmetic and the drawing helpers are pasted from the workbook as source, not restated, so a
        figure here is computed by the same code that computes it there.

        **Cannot be done on this page.** Re-run a parameter that writes into a spreadsheet cell: that
        needs `formulas` and the exercise workbook. Ask a loan-rate question: the workbook's own rule
        allows it only under `shipped-decoupled`, so it is answered by refusing, here and there alike.
        Read the corpus inventory: it queries the task database, and a published page has no business
        carrying file paths from the machine that built it.

        **The claim is narrow, and it is the whole claim:** every number on this page came out of the
        exercise spreadsheet's own runs, and every rate applied to those numbers is arithmetic you can
        move and watch. Nothing here is a second model of the farm. If it disagrees with the live
        workbook, the generator is wrong and belongs regenerated, not edited.
    """
    )


